<!-- Buying guide (unique local copy; facts from this page, manufacturer spec pages, and /guides/) -->
<section class="pt-70 pb-30">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-9 guide-body">
        <h2>Who the Artesian Elite is for</h2>
        <p>The Artesian Elite is the top of our lineup. It's for people buying a hot tub mainly for hydrotherapy: athletes, anyone dealing with sore joints or back tension, and owners who want every seat to feel different. The <strong>DIRECTFLOW Personal Control System</strong> lets each person adjust the jets at their own seat, and the 316L stainless steel H2O PowerFlow jets, dual footblasters and lighting package are all standard.</p>
        <p>With five models from the 4-person Quail Ridge to the 9-person Pelican Bay, there's an Elite for couples and for big families. The compact Quail Ridge still packs 57 jets into about 340 gallons.</p>
        <h2>Electrical and installation</h2>
        <p>Every Elite uses a 5.5 kW titanium heater and multiple jet pumps (the Quail Ridge has four 3.0 BHP jet pumps), so plan on a dedicated 240V circuit from a licensed electrician and a level concrete pad or engineered deck. The spa is WiFi-ready with a worldwide WiFi app module, which is handy for checking on the spa when you're away. Optional <a href="/steps/">Monarch Elite steps</a> come in Mocha, Smoke and Noir.</p>
        <h2>The Elite in a Utah winter</h2>
        <p>Elite spas use full foam insulation with a PermaBase ABS pan and a 5-inch tapered cover, which helps hold heat through cold nights. The large heater recovers quickly after long soaks. Our <a href="/guides/hot-tub-utah-winter/">winter guide</a> covers snow, covers and freeze protection.</p>
        <h2>Compare before you decide</h2>
        <p>Weighing the Elite against an Island Spa with the Elite trim, or against a Nordic? Our <a href="/guides/hot-tub-brands-compared/">brand comparison</a> lays out the differences. We keep display models from every brand we carry at 6905 S State St in Midvale (Mon–Sat, 10 AM–5 PM). Floor models change, so <a href="/contact/">call or message us</a> if you want to sit in a specific model before you visit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

